# A raw NUL byte in src/lib/mentions.ts once made the file binary to every
# grep, hiding its exports from repo-wide search. No attribute here can fix
# that: grep, ripgrep and editors never read this file. What `diff` does is
# keep git itself honest (git diff, git log -p, git blame, git grep show the
# text instead of "Binary files differ") when a control byte slips in. The
# gate that actually rejects such bytes is scripts/check-source-bytes.sh,
# which CI runs before lint.
*.ts   text diff
*.tsx  text diff
*.js   text diff
*.mjs  text diff
*.json text diff
*.md   text diff
*.css  text diff
*.yml  text diff

# Shell scripts run on the Linux production box; a CRLF checkout would turn
# the shebang into "bash\r" and every script into "command not found".
*.sh   text eol=lf diff
